# Ticket 07 device check — Pixel 7 Pro (29131FDH3009SZ), 2026-08-08

## Transcribed, not captured

The two lines below were read live from the device's logcat ring buffer at 19:17, but the
buffer (256 KiB, and the scan had just filled it) rotated past them before they could be
redirected to a file. They are transcribed verbatim from that read. Everything after this
section is a live capture and is not transcribed.

Driver's scan, detection toggled OFF, cold library:

    08-08 19:13:18.757  I ReactNativeJS: [series] detection is off — no series were read or written
    08-08 19:13:18.761  I ReactNativeJS: [scan] 189638ms total · 3461 files, 3461 new (54.3ms/new file) — enumerate 1261ms · existing-urls 35ms · process 188097ms · cleanup 227ms · detect 3ms

What this closes, on its own:

- **OFF stops future detection.** The guard fires and says so, and `detect 3ms` against the
  338 ms ticket 06 measured for a real run is the early return being real rather than
  asserted — it returns before its first read, so there was nothing to write.
- The library is **3461 files, all new**, so this device starts from a clean library with
  **zero detected series**, which is the correct starting state for the retroactive button.

